diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 344f452..f9369e1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,6 +4,16 @@ Pulse is an internal market-insights dashboard. It shows key figures, a sortable
 
 Routes: `/` dashboard, `/portfolio`, `/trades`, `/instruments/:symbol`, `/clients`, `/reports`, `/settings`.
 
+Portfolio: the summary cards show signed P&L and day change ("+$121.6K"); the holdings table can be narrowed to one book with the "Book" filter (the totals row and its weight follow the filter); "Show values in" switches every money value on the page (cards, market value, P&L, totals, allocation legend, P&L by book) between USD, EUR and GBP at today's FX rates, while prices and average cost stay in the instrument's own currency; a "P&L by book" panel lists every book with its positions, market value and unrealized P&L; and "Export holdings" downloads the holdings shown as CSV, values in the chosen currency.
+
+Clients: the list is sorted A to Z and searches by name, contact or region; the drawer shows AUM in whole dollars. Client notes support `**bold**` and `[label](https://...)` links; anything else, HTML included, shows as typed, and only http and https links become links. Notes can be pinned to the top ("Pin" / "Unpin"). Notes are stored per client under `pulse.client-notes.<client id>`; notes saved before pinning read as unpinned, and an unreadable value reads as no notes.
+
+Reports: a "Search reports" box filters the current tab by title or author; each report reads "Oct 27, 2026 · A. Moreau · 6 pages", and scheduled ones "Due Oct 30, 2026 · L. Duarte".
+
+Trades: notionals are formatted as amounts with cents, so a cancelled trade reads "$0.00" in the blotter, the dashboard and the trade drawer.
+
+Settings: the "Report digest" choice (Off, Daily, Weekly) replaces the weekly digest switch. Settings are saved under `pulse.settings`; an old save with `weeklyDigest` keeps its choice (on is Weekly, off is Off), and an unreadable save falls back to the defaults.
+
 All data is mocked: typed fetchers in `src/api` read JSON files in `src/data` after a short artificial delay.
 
 ## Run it
